# The loader's fixes (U6c): each "did you mean" as the change that makes it, as the editor's
# problems panel offers it. A misspelt word is set; a misspelt key is renamed.

# The sample with three typos: a drift policy, a key and a faction.
validate crates/cli/tests/fixtures/worlds/typos
fixes crates/cli/tests/fixtures/worlds/typos

# A world that loads has nothing to fix, and a syntax error has no suggestion.
assert fixes content/sample == content/sample loads: nothing to fix
assert fixes crates/cli/tests/fixtures/worlds/unparsed_balance == crates/cli/tests/fixtures/worlds/unparsed_balance doesn't load: 1 problem, none with a fix
